    "long_instructions": "# Stopwatch\r\n\r\n## Do This\r\n\r\n1. Find where to write your `while` loop inside the `runStopwatch()` function.\r\n2. Use AI to help you complete the `while` loop so that it keeps counting up while the button is held down and stops when the button is released.\r\n3. Test your stopwatch to make sure it starts when pressed, stops when released, and doesn’t become an infinite loop.\r\n\r\n<details> \r\n  <summary>Need help? Ask the AI Tutor.</summary> \r\n    <ol> \r\n      <li>How do I make the loop keep running while <code>running</code> is true?</li> \r\n      <li>How do I update the time so it increases each second?</li> \r\n      <li>How do I stop the loop when the user lets go of the button?</li> \r\n    </ol> \r\n</details>"
